			<div class="content" id="post-content-3563839">
									

<p>Upon reading this article, I am struck almost immediately by how closely it resembles <a href="/scp-1739">SCP-1739</a>, from a Dell laptop catalyzing the destruction of another universe to a researcher talking to his alternate counterpart . Unfortunately, the conversation between David 1 and David A is far less compelling, as is the general anomaly.</p>
<p>Furthermore, the <a href="/scp-2317">SCP-2317</a>-esque escalation fails to grab me, though the subversion of the final object class is commendable. The connection to Gamers Against Weed is unnecessary at best and suspension-breakingly absurd at worst. Finally, the animated text does absolutely nothing to enhance the reading - the fact that you kept the debugging skip tool shows that it actually hinders it.</p>
<p>The effort put into the presentation is admirable; the story being told, however, is not.</p>

