			<div class="content" id="post-content-3564076">
									

<p>GAW being able to casually hack the Foundation database is, yeah, kind of ridiculous, but I was able to accept it while I read, so I don't think it was a problem.</p>
<p>I really like the use of increasing clearance levels to reveal more of the story. And it isn't just &quot;here's more info every time&quot;; the major change in that last one moves the story ahead, and there's still expungement! I mean, I've seen it before, but this is an example of it used well, and I'll really never get tired of it. A few things:</p>
<ul>
<li>We don't use electrons to make anything. That wording caught me off guard.</li>
<li>In the interview, Graham 2 says &quot;you were in the lead&quot; twice.</li>
<li>What's with &quot;apon&quot;? The first looked like a typo, the second makes me think it's indicative of something, but I can't figure out what.</li>
<li>And there's a big void at the end of clearance 5 that doesn't seem to exist for any purpose. Not sure what could be done about that.</li>
</ul>
<p>In all, a pretty good skip with cool execution, nicely done. :)</p>

